BT /F1 11 Tf 72 710 Td (Pacing is the deliberate control of reading speed and rest. Faster is not always better.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 695 Td (A reader who races through a dense page may need to go back, which costs more time than) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 680 Td (reading carefully once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 72 649 Td (Signals of fatigue) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 629 Td (Three observable signals often appear together before a reader gives up. Reading time) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 614 Td (per chunk rises. Checkpoint answers become short or skipped. Navigation starts moving) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 599 Td (backward as the reader loses the thread.) Tj ET
